# steam_project — agent workflow

Monorepo: `app_fetcher/` (Steam data API, Sorbet, Sidekiq) and `app_core/`
(Turbo/Stimulus + React dashboard island). Shared stack in `docker-compose.yml`.

## Shared docs (Claude + Cursor)

Canonical paths — both tools read and write the same files:

- `agent/adr/` — ADRs (`fetcher/`, `core/`, plus `base.md`)
- `agent/styleguides/` — conventions (top-level shared; `fetcher/`; `core/`)
- `agent/US/` — user stories
- `agent/plans/` — development plans

Skills: `.cursor/skills/` (this tool). Claude uses `.claude/skills/` with the
same pipeline. Shared docs live only under `agent/`.

## CI & git hooks

- CI lives at the repo root: `.github/workflows/ci.yml` (GitHub reads no
  other location). Jobs: `linters` (RuboCop, Sorbet `srb tc`, Brakeman,
  bundler-audit, ESLint, Prettier), `tests` (RSpec ×2, Vitest), and a
  non-blocking `coverage` job (Codecov). Everything runs through
  `docker compose` via `docker-compose.ci.yml`. See
  `agent/styleguides/ci-and-coverage.md`.
- Git hooks use `lefthook`: run `npm install` once at the repo root (its
  `prepare` script runs `lefthook install`). `pre-commit` lints staged
  Ruby/JS; `commit-msg` enforces the `[Scope] Imperative summary`
  convention. See `agent/styleguides/git-hooks.md`.
- Each app's `bin/ci` is the local equivalent of CI — keep it aligned.

## Development pipeline

For any non-trivial change (new behavior, business-logic bug fix, new
integration — not one-line fixes or pure formatting), follow this order:

1. `research-codebase`
2. `create-dev-plan` → writes `agent/plans/<slug>.md` (`status: draft`)
3. `styleguides-check` → may require `create-styleguide` /
   `create-styleguide-from-scratch` / `update-styleguide`; plan becomes
   `blocked` or `styleguide-checked`
4. `implement-plan` → TDD; plan becomes `implemented`

Do not jump to implementation for non-trivial work. If a later stage
contradicts an earlier one, go back rather than improvising.

Plan status flow: `draft` → `blocked` / `styleguide-checked` → `implemented`.

## Styleguide / ADR scope

- `agent/styleguides/base.md`, `agent/adr/base.md` — format templates
- top-level `agent/styleguides/*.md` — cross-app conventions
- `agent/styleguides/fetcher|core/`, `agent/adr/fetcher|core/` — per-app
- Deviations go in `agent/styleguides/fix_me.md`, not fixed ad hoc as
  alternate conventions

Default new guides/ADRs to the per-app folder when unsure.
